.Dd July 30, 2026
.Dt LIBCAPBUNDLE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm libcapbundle
.Nd parse and validate capability bundles
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libcapbundle
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In libcapbundle.h
.Ft int
.Fn capbundle_open "const char *path" "struct capbundle **bp" "char *errbuf" "size_t errlen"
.Ft void
.Fn capbundle_close "struct capbundle *b"
.Ft int
.Fn capbundle_verify "const struct capbundle *b" "char *errbuf" "size_t errlen"
.Ft int
.Fn capbundle_check_startup_cycles "struct capbundle **bundles" "unsigned nbundles" "char *errbuf" "size_t errlen"
.Ft int
.Fn capbundle_scan_dir "const char *path" "capbundle_scan_cb cb" "void *arg"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
parses root-owned
.Pa .cap
application directories for
.Xr serviced 8 .
A bundle contains executables in
.Pa bin
and strict UCL service declarations in
.Pa etc .
.Pp
Each declaration identifies its
.Va bundle_id ,
.Va program ,
zero or more global names in
.Va provides ,
and delegated capabilities.
A service with at least one
.Va provides
entry is activated on demand by a lookup of any provided name.
A declaration without
.Va provides
is an eager boot task.
Activation is derived and cannot be selected with a manifest option.
.Pp
The optional
.Va components
field is either one string or an array containing the distinct literals
.Dq filesystem
and
.Dq network .
These request mandatory process-local authority replacements constructed
before exec.
There are no provider, version, lifetime, sharing, optionality, or options
fields, and local components do not participate in global service selection.
.Pp
A process may advertise up to eight global names.
The names identify independent endpoints but map to the same service runtime.
Activation is runtime-based, while connection routing remains exact-name
based.
.Pp
Parsing rejects unknown keys, wrong types, duplicate names or components,
invalid paths and claims, reserved environment variables, malformed bundle
identity, and entries beyond fixed limits.
.Fn capbundle_verify
also verifies executables and internal consistency.
.Fn capbundle_check_startup_cycles
validates internal component-factory startup edges across bundle sets.
.Sh ACCESSORS
The public header provides accessors for bundle identity, version, author,
path and name; service count, program and derived runtime label; provided
names; derived activation state; literal arguments and environment;
and conversion to
.Vt struct svc_manifest .
Returned strings remain owned by the bundle.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Functions returning
.Vt int
return zero on success and -1 on failure.
When supplied, the error buffer receives a diagnostic suitable for
administrative tools.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libservice 3 ,
.Xr serviced 5 ,
.Xr serviced 8
